{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>To wash upon the river.</b> To wash in the river. A parallel: על שדה הארץ יחשב, על חרבך תחיה, על הבתים אשר יאכלו אותו בהם." "<b>And her maidens.</b> It mentions them here because it is about to say ותשלח את אמתה — she is one of the maidens." "<b>Walking.</b> To die. And so it says: הנה אנכי הולך למות. As stated in the first chapter of Sotah: Gabriel came and struck them to the ground because they protested against Pharaoh's daughter, except for one whom he left her, for it is not the way of a king's daughter to stand alone. That is ותשלח את אמתה, her maidservant. For the alef has a hatef-patach."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:56:35.072248579Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}